{
  "name": "flea",
  "_about": "The cat flea (Ctenocephalides felis), 2.5 mm long: flattened sideways -- tall and narrow, glossy dark reddish brown; a small rounded head with a comb of black spines along the cheek and another behind the pronotum; short clubbed antennae lying in a groove; a piercing beak; a big abdomen of overlapping plates bristling with backward hairs; the hind legs huge, their coxae broad plates, for leaps of 30 cm. Coat: the human flea (no combs, paler). Written whole by tools/creaturegen/rework/insects/bugs.py on insectlib.py (jointed legs on a walking gait, the antennae on bones of their own that wave).",
